{% include 'components/lenders-data.njk' %}

{% macro ltvDisplay(v, key, ltv) -%}
  {%- if ltv[key + 'Display'] -%}{{ ltv[key + 'Display'] }}
  {%- elif v === null or v === undefined -%}not published
  {%- else -%}{{ (v * 100) | round(1) }}%
  {%- endif -%}
{%- endmacro %}

{% macro drawdown(open, thr) -%}{{ (100 * (1 - open / thr)) | round }}{%- endmacro %}

<section class="hero">
    <h1>Borrowing against bitcoin: <em>the lenders</em></h1>
    <div class="hero-subtitle">Every lender that takes bitcoin as collateral, one card each: the published rate, the loan-to-value lines, the price that triggers them today, who holds the coins, the terms, and the catch.</div>
    <p class="subtitle">Nothing here is ranked or recommended. The figures are what each lender publishes, dated; where a lender publishes nothing the card says so. The argument for and against borrowing at all is on <a href="/borrowing-against-your-stack">Borrowing Against Your Stack</a>; this page is the map of who offers it.</p>
</section>

<main class="content-area">
    {% include 'components/tool-framing.njk' %}

    {#- The levers: the seven things every card measures, for a reader who has
        not met the vocabulary. JM, 2026-09-30: the page is complex and the cards
        were too casual about it; orient the reader before the cards. Always
        visible, compact; the §6.13 tooltips carry the terms that recur below. -#}
    <section class="ln-levers" id="levers" aria-labelledby="leversTitle">
        <h2 id="leversTitle" class="ln-levers-title">Before the cards: the seven things every card measures</h2>
        <p class="ln-levers-lede">A bitcoin-backed loan is simpler than its vocabulary. You pledge bitcoin, you borrow dollars against it, and the only question that matters is what happens when the price moves. Every card describes that with the same seven measures.</p>
        <dl class="ln-levers-grid">
            <div><dt>Loan-to-value (LTV)</dt><dd>How much you borrow compared with what your bitcoin is worth. Borrow $50,000 against $100,000 of bitcoin and you are at 50%. The loan is fixed in dollars, so when the price falls the percentage rises; every line on a card is one of these percentages.</dd></div>
            <div><dt>The margin call</dt><dd>The percentage at which the lender asks you to add bitcoin or repay part of the loan. The <em>cure window</em> is how long you get: 72 hours at Strike, 24 at Arch and Unchained, no fixed time at several others, and none at all where the lender simply sells.</dd></div>
            <div><dt>Liquidation</dt><dd>The percentage at which the lender sells. <em>Partial</em> means it sells only enough to bring the loan back to its opening level; <em>total</em> means the whole collateral goes. The multisig lenders hand the bitcoin itself to the lender; the DeFi markets let anyone sell it and keep a penalty.</dd></div>
            <div><dt>The trigger price</dt><dd>Each line turned into a bitcoin price: today&rsquo;s price &times; the opening LTV &divide; the line. A loan at 50% with an 85% line is sold after a 41% fall, whatever the price is today. Interest added to the loan moves the real trigger a little higher. The control above switches every card to a loan-to-value of your own.</dd></div>
            <div><dt>The rate</dt><dd><em>APR</em> is the yearly cost, including any opening fee where the lender quotes it that way. <em>Fixed</em> holds for the term; <em>variable</em> moves. Most lenders charge less for bigger loans; SALT charges by how much of the value you borrow; Cadena is paid in bitcoin at the end.</dd></div>
            <div><dt>Your coins</dt><dd>Who holds the bitcoin while the loan runs, whether you can watch the address, and whether the lender may lend it on to anyone else. That last practice, <em>rehypothecation</em>, is what sank Celsius, BlockFi and Voyager in 2022: the collateral was lent to borrowers who failed. Each card says what the lender promises.</dd></div>
            <div><dt>Term and repayment</dt><dd>How long the loan runs and the shape of the payments: interest monthly or at the end, the principal at the end, or no end date at all. Some loans can&rsquo;t be repaid early: Firefish still charges the full term&rsquo;s interest, Cadena is locked.</dd></div>
            <div><dt>&ldquo;Not published&rdquo;</dt><dd>A value, not a gap in our reading. Where a lender withholds a figure (Figure&rsquo;s liquidation line, Kraken Borrow&rsquo;s rate, Lava&rsquo;s liquidation price) the card says so rather than guessing, and that is itself something to know about the lender.</dd></div>
        </dl>
    </section>

    {#- The dated change log (lenders v2 C, JM's rulings 2026-10-01). Rendered from
        src/_data/lenderLog.json via lenderLogIndex.js; every monthly re-read is
        logged even when nothing changed, so a quiet month reads as checked, not
        neglected. Procedure: MONTHLY_REFRESH_CHECKLIST §7.6. -#}
    <section class="ln-log" id="what-changed" aria-labelledby="lnLogTitle">
        <div class="ln-log-head">
            <h2 id="lnLogTitle" class="ln-log-title">What changed</h2>
            <p class="ln-log-lede">Lenders change their terms more often than anything else on this site. Every card is re-read in full against the lender&rsquo;s own pages each month, and every check is logged here, newest first, with whatever it found.{% if lenderLogIndex.nextCheckLabel %} Next check: <strong>{{ lenderLogIndex.nextCheckLabel }}</strong>.{% endif %}</p>
        </div>
        {% macro logItem(e) -%}
            <li class="ln-log-item ln-log-{{ e.kind }}">
                <time datetime="{{ e.date }}">{{ e.label }}</time>
                <span class="ln-log-who">{% if e.lender %}<a href="#lender-{{ e.lender }}">{{ e.name }}</a>{% elif e.kind == 'check' %}Cards checked{% else %}This page{% endif %}</span>
                <span class="ln-log-text">{{ e.text | safe }}{% if e.source %} <a class="ln-log-src" href="{{ e.source }}" rel="nofollow noopener" target="_blank">Source <span aria-hidden="true">&nearr;</span></a>{% endif %}</span>
            </li>
        {%- endmacro %}
        <ol class="ln-log-list">
            {% for e in lenderLogIndex.entries %}{% if loop.index <= 5 %}{{ logItem(e) }}{% endif %}{% endfor %}
        </ol>
        {% if lenderLogIndex.entries.length > 5 %}
        <details class="ln-log-more">
            <summary>Earlier ({{ lenderLogIndex.entries.length - 5 }})</summary>
            <ol class="ln-log-list">
                {% for e in lenderLogIndex.entries %}{% if loop.index > 5 %}{{ logItem(e) }}{% endif %}{% endfor %}
            </ol>
        </details>
        {% endif %}
    </section>

    {#- The controls sit with the cards they change (JM, 2026-10-01: the price,
        the date read and the trigger control felt separated from the data).
        One panel: the context line, the filters, the trigger control. -#}
    <div class="ln-live ln-controls" id="lnLive">
        <div class="ln-live-price" aria-live="polite">Bitcoin <strong id="lnPrice">&mdash;</strong> <span class="ln-live-src" id="lnPriceSrc"></span> &middot; each card read from the lender&rsquo;s own pages, <strong>{{ lenderLogIndex.checkedRange or lenders.asOfLabel }}</strong>; the date is on every card</div>
        <div class="ln-filters" id="lnFilters" aria-label="Filters">
            <button class="ln-chip on" type="button" data-filter="all">All</button>
            <button class="ln-chip" type="button" data-filter="bitcoinOnly">Bitcoin only</button>
            <button class="ln-chip" type="button" data-filter="noRehyp">States no rehypothecation</button>
            <button class="ln-chip" type="button" data-filter="holdKey">You hold a key</button>
            <button class="ln-chip" type="button" data-filter="noPriceLiq">No-price-liquidation option</button>
            <button class="ln-chip" type="button" data-filter="under5k">Under $5,000</button>
            <label class="ln-state"><span>Available in</span>
                <select id="lnState" aria-label="US state">
                    <option value="">any state</option>
                    {% set states = ['AL','AK','AZ','AR','CA','CO','CT','DE','DC','FL','GA','HI','ID','IL','IN','IA','KS','KY','LA','ME','MD','MA','MI','MN','MS','MO','MT','NE','NV','NH','NJ','NM','NY','NC','ND','OH','OK','OR','PA','PR','RI','SC','SD','TN','TX','UT','VT','VA','WA','WV','WI','WY'] %}
                    {% for s in states %}<option value="{{ s }}">{{ s }}</option>{% endfor %}
                </select>
            </label>
            <span class="ln-count" id="lnCount"></span>
        </div>
        <div class="ln-live-ctl" role="group" aria-label="The loan the trigger prices describe">
            <span class="ln-live-ctl-label">Trigger prices if you borrow<span class="help-tip" tabindex="0">?<span class="tip-content"><strong>Which loan the cards describe.</strong> Each card works out the bitcoin price at which a loan would reach the lender&rsquo;s warning line and its sale line. By default that is the largest loan each lender allows. Choose <em>a share I pick</em> to put the same loan through every lender: borrowing a smaller share of your bitcoin&rsquo;s value means the price can fall further before anything happens. You don&rsquo;t need a loan to use it; it is a what-if, and it changes only the trigger sentences.</span></span></span>
            <label class="ln-radio"><input type="radio" name="lnMode" value="max" checked> the most each lender allows</label>
            <label class="ln-radio"><input type="radio" name="lnMode" value="own"> a share I pick</label>
            <span class="ln-own" id="lnOwnWrap">
                <input type="range" id="lnOwnLtv" min="10" max="80" step="1" value="35" aria-label="The share of your bitcoin&rsquo;s value borrowed, percent">
                <strong id="lnOwnLtvOut">35%</strong><span class="ln-own-of">of your bitcoin&rsquo;s value</span>
            </span>
        </div>
        <p class="ln-live-hint" id="lnOwnHint">Each card shows its lender&rsquo;s own largest loan. To compare lenders on the same loan, pick a share of your bitcoin&rsquo;s value. It&rsquo;s a what-if; no loan needed.</p>
    </div>

    {% for g in lenders.groups %}
    <section class="ln-group" id="{{ g.id }}" data-group="{{ g.id }}">
        <h2 class="ln-grp">{{ g.title }}</h2>
        <p class="ln-grp-sub">{% if g.qualifier %}<span class="ln-tag qual">{{ g.qualifier }}</span> {% endif %}{{ g.sub | replace('Borrowing Against Your Stack → mortgages', '<a href="/bitcoin-backed-mortgages">Bitcoin-Backed Mortgages</a>') | safe }}</p>
        <div class="ln-grid">
        {% for l in lenders.lenders %}{% if l.group == g.id %}
            {% set ltv = l.ltv %}
            <article class="ln-card" id="lender-{{ l.id }}" data-id="{{ l.id }}"
                     data-open="{{ ltv.open if ltv.open !== null and ltv.open !== undefined else '' }}"
                     data-ref="{{ ltv.reference if ltv.reference else '' }}"
                     data-call="{{ ltv.call if ltv.call !== null and ltv.call !== undefined else '' }}"
                     data-liq="{{ ltv.liq if ltv.liq !== null and ltv.liq !== undefined else '' }}"
                     data-bitcoin-only="{{ 'y' if l.filters.bitcoinOnly else 'n' }}"
                     data-no-rehyp="{{ 'y' if l.filters.noRehyp else 'n' }}"
                     data-hold-key="{{ 'y' if l.filters.holdKey else 'n' }}"
                     data-no-price-liq="{{ 'y' if l.filters.noPriceLiq else 'n' }}"
                     data-under5k="{{ 'y' if l.filters.under5k else 'n' }}"
                     data-states-type="{{ l.states.type }}"
                     data-states-list="{{ (l.states.list | join(',')) if l.states.list else '' }}"
                     data-states-rest="{{ l.states.rest or '' }}">
                <div class="ln-state-flag" id="flag-{{ l.id }}" aria-live="polite"></div>
                <div class="ln-head">
                    <div class="ln-head-text">
                        <h3 class="ln-name">{{ l.name }}</h3>
                        <div class="ln-model">{{ l.model }}</div>
                    </div>
                    <div class="ln-chips">
                        {% if l.bitcoinOnly %}<span class="ln-tag yes">&#10003; Bitcoin only</span>{% else %}<span class="ln-tag no">Not bitcoin only &middot; {{ l.otherCollateral }}</span>{% endif %}
                        {% if l.qualifier %}<span class="ln-tag qual">{{ l.qualifier }}</span>{% endif %}
                        {%- set lg = lenderLogIndex.byLender[l.id] %}{% if lg and lg.length %}<a class="ln-tag ln-changed" href="#what-changed" data-log-date="{{ lg[0].date }}" data-log-type="{{ lg[0].type }}" data-log-label="{{ lg[0].label }}"{% if lg[0].changes %} data-log-changes="{{ lg[0].changes | dump | escape }}"{% endif %} hidden><span class="ln-pulse" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="ln-changed-t"></span></a>{% endif %}
                    </div>
                </div>
                <div class="ln-rate" data-f="rate"><b{% if l.rate.np %} class="np"{% endif %}>{{ l.rate.headline }}</b><span>{{ l.rate.note | safe }}</span></div>
                <div class="ln-ltv">
                    <div data-f="open"><div class="k">Opens at<span class="help-tip" tabindex="0">?<span class="tip-content"><strong>Opens at.</strong> The most you can borrow as a share of your bitcoin&rsquo;s value on the day the loan starts. A loan is fixed in dollars, so this share rises as the price falls.</span></span></div>{% set _d = ltvDisplay(ltv.open, 'open', ltv) | trim %}<div class="v{% if _d.length > 11 %} xlong{% elif _d.length > 7 %} long{% endif %}">{{ _d }}</div><div class="p">{{ ltv.openNote | safe }}</div></div>
                    <div class="call" data-f="call"><div class="k">{{ ltv.callLabel }}<span class="help-tip" tabindex="0">?<span class="tip-content"><strong>The warning line.</strong> The share at which the lender asks you to add bitcoin or repay part of the loan, in whatever words the lender uses (margin call, alert, violation, a health status). The small line under it says how long you get.</span></span></div>{% set _d = ltvDisplay(ltv.call, 'call', ltv) | trim %}<div class="v{% if _d.length > 11 %} xlong{% elif _d.length > 7 %} long{% endif %}">{{ _d }}</div><div class="p">{{ ltv.callNote | safe }}</div></div>
                    <div class="liq" data-f="liq"><div class="k">Liquidates<span class="help-tip help-tip-right" tabindex="0">?<span class="tip-content"><strong>Liquidates.</strong> The share at which the lender sells, or hands the bitcoin to the lender. <em>Partial</em> means only enough to restore the loan; <em>total</em> means all of it. &ldquo;Not published&rdquo; means the lender doesn&rsquo;t say.</span></span></div>{% set _d = ltvDisplay(ltv.liq, 'liq', ltv) | trim %}<div class="v{% if _d.length > 11 %} xlong{% elif _d.length > 7 %} long{% endif %}">{{ _d }}</div><div class="p">{{ ltv.liqNote | safe }}</div></div>
                </div>
                <p class="ln-trig" id="trig-{{ l.id }}" data-f="trig">
                    {%- if l.trig.mode == 'auto' -%}
                        {%- set base = ltv.open if ltv.open else ltv.reference -%}
                        {%- if base and (ltv.call or ltv.liq) -%}
                            {%- if ltv.open %}A maximum loan ({{ (ltv.open * 100) | round }}% LTV){% else %}A 50% loan ({{ l.name }} doesn&rsquo;t publish a maximum){% endif %}
                            {%- if ltv.call %} {{ ltv.callVerb }} after a <strong>{{ drawdown(base, ltv.call) }}% fall</strong>{% endif %}
                            {%- if ltv.call and ltv.liq %} and{% endif %}
                            {%- if ltv.liq %} {{ ltv.liqVerb }} after a <strong>{{ drawdown(base, ltv.liq) }}% fall</strong>{% endif %}.
                        {%- endif %}
                        {%- if l.trig.extra %} {{ l.trig.extra | safe }}{% endif -%}
                    {%- else -%}
                        {{ l.trig.static | safe }}
                    {%- endif -%}
                </p>
                <div class="ln-pair">
                    <div class="plus"><span class="l">Distinguishing</span>{{ l.distinguishing | safe }}</div>
                    <div class="catch"><span class="l">The catch</span>{{ l.catch | safe }}</div>
                </div>
                {#- The rest of the card is one click away. Without JS the <details>
                    expands in place; with JS the same block opens in the large-type
                    dialog (#lnDialog) and the URL gains #lender-<id>, so a single
                    lender is linkable and Back closes it. -#}
                <div class="ln-links">
                    {%- set ck = lenderLogIndex.checked[l.id] %}{% if ck %}<span class="ln-checked" title="Last read against {{ l.name }}&rsquo;s own pages">Checked <time datetime="{{ ck.date }}">{{ ck.label }}</time></span>{% endif %}
                    <a class="ln-site" href="{{ l.site }}" rel="nofollow noopener" target="_blank">{{ l.name }}&rsquo;s own page <span aria-hidden="true">&nearr;</span></a>
                </div>
                <details class="ln-more" data-id="{{ l.id }}">
                    <summary class="ln-more-btn"><span>How it works, terms, custody, where, sources</span><span class="ln-more-arrow" aria-hidden="true">&rsaquo;</span></summary>
                    <div class="ln-more-body">
                        <div class="ln-how"><span class="l">How this loan works</span><p>{{ l.how | safe }}</p><a class="ln-site ln-site-big" href="{{ l.site }}" rel="nofollow noopener" target="_blank">Read it in {{ l.name }}&rsquo;s own words <span aria-hidden="true">&nearr;</span></a></div>
                        <dl class="ln-dl">
                            <dt>Your coins<span class="help-tip" tabindex="0">?<span class="tip-content"><strong>Your coins.</strong> Who holds the bitcoin during the loan, whether you can watch the address on the blockchain, and whether the lender may lend it on (rehypothecation). The 2022 failures were all failures of this.</span></span></dt><dd data-f="coins">{{ l.coins | safe }}</dd>
                            <dt>Terms</dt><dd data-f="terms">{{ l.terms | safe }}</dd>
                            <dt>Minimum</dt><dd data-f="minimum">{{ l.minimum | safe }}</dd>
                            <dt>Where</dt><dd data-f="where">{{ l.where | safe }}</dd>
                            <dt>Track record</dt><dd data-f="track">{{ l.track | safe }}</dd>
                            {%- set lg = lenderLogIndex.byLender[l.id] %}{% if lg and lg.length %}
                            <dt>Changes logged</dt><dd><ul class="ln-hist">{% for e in lg %}<li><time datetime="{{ e.date }}">{{ e.label }}</time> {{ e.text | safe }}{% if e.source %} <a href="{{ e.source }}" rel="nofollow noopener" target="_blank">source</a>{% endif %}</li>{% endfor %}</ul></dd>{% endif %}
                        </dl>
                        <div class="ln-foot">Sources, read {{ l.asOf }}: {% for s in l.sources %}<a href="{{ s }}" rel="nofollow noopener" target="_blank">{{ s | replace('https://', '') | replace('http://', '') | replace('www.', '') | truncate(44, true, '…') }}</a>{% if not loop.last %} · {% endif %}{% endfor %}</div>
                        <a class="ln-depth" href="{{ l.depth.href }}">Depth: {{ l.depth.label }} &rarr;</a>
                    </div>
                </details>
            </article>
        {% endif %}{% endfor %}
        </div>
    </section>
    {% endfor %}

    <p class="ln-empty" id="lnEmpty" hidden>No lender matches every filter. Each chip narrows the list; clear one.</p>

    <dialog class="ln-dialog" id="lnDialog" aria-label="Lender detail">
        <div class="ln-dialog-bar"><span class="ln-dialog-crumb" id="lnDialogCrumb"></span><button type="button" class="ln-dialog-close" id="lnDialogClose" aria-label="Close">&times;</button></div>
        <div class="ln-dialog-body" id="lnDialogBody"></div>
    </dialog>

    <section class="ln-prose" id="how-to-read">
        <h2>How to read a card</h2>
        <p>A card&rsquo;s face carries what you decide with: the marks, the rate, the three lines, the trigger sentence, what distinguishes the lender and what the catch is. The row at the foot opens the rest in larger type: how the loan works in plain words, who holds your coins, the terms, the minimum, where the lender operates, its record, and the dated sources, with a link to the lender&rsquo;s own page so you can read its description in its own words. The address bar then names the lender, so a single detail can be linked to.</p>
        <p><strong>The marks.</strong> <span class="ln-tag yes">&#10003; Bitcoin only</span> means the lender takes no other collateral; <span class="ln-tag no">Not bitcoin only</span> names what else shares its risk engine. The dashed <span class="ln-tag qual">qualifier</span> flags a product that isn&rsquo;t an open-use loan against your bitcoin: buying power that can&rsquo;t leave an exchange, a token standing for bitcoin, a mortgage that buys a house, a contract in which you sell your own bitcoin for the cash.</p>
        <p><strong>Groups, not ranks.</strong> Cards sit with others of the same model and alphabetically within it. There is no sort by rate and no best badge, because an order reads as a recommendation. The lowest rate on the page today belongs to a protocol with no one to call; one of the highest to the lender that has never lost a coin in nine years. Both facts are on their cards.</p>
    </section>

    <section class="ln-prose" id="what-this-is-not">
        <h2>What this page is, and isn&rsquo;t</h2>
        <p>It is a description of a market as the lenders themselves describe it, read on the date each card carries and re-read monthly (rates move most; Ledn&rsquo;s standard rate rose from 10.99% to 11.49% between March and September 2026, and Strike&rsquo;s 7.75% floor left its calculator). It carries no affiliate or referral links and no lender has paid for a card. It is not a recommendation to borrow, or to borrow from anyone: the case for and against is on <a href="/borrowing-against-your-stack">Borrowing Against Your Stack</a>, whose own answer, for most readers most of the time, is probably not.</p>
        <p>Three lenders&rsquo; own pages disagree with themselves (Arch on states and rates, Debifi on the liquidation fee, Milo on its margin-call trigger). The cards say so rather than picking a side; the lender&rsquo;s app quote is the only figure that binds. If a card is wrong or a term has moved, the <a href="#pfWrap">feedback form</a> below reaches the person who maintains it.</p>
    </section>
</main>
